#
# 'DATA' is not an ADIF mode (rickmurphy.net's validator rejected NY4I's CQ WW
# SSB export). ADIF has no generic data mode, so -- NY4I's ruling, as issue
# 457 already did for Digital with no submode -- such a QSO is written as
# MODE RTTY, with <APP_TR4W_MODE_ASSUMED:1>Y so TR4W's own import restores the
# unknown data mode, and one free-text header line before the first tag
# counting them. ref.adi is D7-written and NEVER regenerated, so the records
# and the header line are pinned here as the exact expected difference.
